# Account env: $SDLCA_SPAWN_HOME/accounts/<account>/env   (the kit sources it as shell: mode 0600, yours alone)
OWNER=alice                                  # the Spawn user this agent account works for
SPAWN_USERNAME=alice_helper                  # this agent account's own Spawn username
SPAWN_TOKEN_FILE=/home/you/.sdlca/spawn/accounts/alice/token

# REQUIRED before any agent runs. The command that performs one agent turn; the prompt arrives on stdin.
# Nothing runs until you choose one (the listener refuses to start without it).
#
# Start with the narrowest option that does the job. Read docs/security-model.md before choosing.
# Every Claude Code example passes --setting-sources user. In print mode (-p) nothing asks before it loads a folder's own settings, so a
# hook in a world's .claude/settings.json or a server in its .mcp.json would run a command on this machine, before any tool rule
# applies, and anyone who can push to a world can add them. The option loads only your own user settings. Keep it (docs/security-model.md).
#   Read-only helper (can read the world's files and answer in chat; cannot edit or run anything else):
#     SDLCA_AGENT_CMD='claude -p --setting-sources user --allowedTools "Read" "Glob" "Grep" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-say *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-api GET *)"'
#   Read-only with sight (the read-only helper, plus sdlca-look: it can take a picture of a world this account serves. The agent's body
#   is in the world for the length of a look, and the picture goes to your model provider. See docs/security-model.md):
#     SDLCA_AGENT_CMD='claude -p --setting-sources user --allowedTools "Read" "Glob" "Grep" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-say *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-api GET *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-look *)"'
#   Builder with an explicit tool allowlist (verified with Claude Code 2.1; adjust to your needs). Edits are
#   allowed; shell commands are limited to the ones listed. $SDLCA_CODE_DIR is expanded when the command runs.
#     SDLCA_AGENT_CMD='claude -p --setting-sources user --permission-mode acceptEdits --allowedTools "Bash(git *)" "Bash(spawn *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-say *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-api *)" "Bash($SDLCA_CODE_DIR/bin/sdlca-look *)"'
#   Full autonomy: the agent can run any command as you. Only for a machine and an owner you fully trust.
#     SDLCA_AGENT_CMD='claude -p --setting-sources user --permission-mode bypassPermissions'
# Any CLI that reads a prompt on stdin works (Codex, OpenCode, Cursor agent, ...): see docs/configuration.md.
# SDLCA_AGENT_CMD=

# Optional
# SDLCA_AGENT_TIMEOUT=1800                   # seconds before a turn is stopped (frees the per-world lock)
# SDLCA_LOCK_WAIT=3600                       # seconds a turn waits for the world's lock before it is kept for replay
# SDLCA_REFRESH_TIMEOUT=60                   # seconds each git call may take when the kit brings a world clone up to date before a turn (0 turns it off)
# SDLCA_MAX_RUNS_PER_HOUR=20                 # cap on agent turns per hour for this account (0 turns the cap off)
# SDLCA_PRESENCE_TTL=3600                    # how long /spawn keeps the agent's body in a world when you give no ttl, 10 to 14400 seconds
# SDLCA_LOOK_TIMEOUT=240                     # seconds a look (sdlca-look: the join and the pictures) may take, 1 to 3600; the body leaves when it ends. A software renderer draws nothing until the world has loaded (a minute or more), and the look waits for it
# SDLCA_LOOK_POLL=10                         # seconds a look waits before it tries again when the picture is blank, 1 to 300
# SDLCA_LOOK_SETTLE=20                       # seconds a look waits, after a real picture that came late, for the scene to fill in before the last picture, 0 to 300
# SDLCA_BODY_POLL=10                         # seconds between the checks on a body's sculpt (sdlca-body), 1 to 300
# SDLCA_SAY_MAX_LINES=8                      # longest reply, in chat lines of at most 200 characters
# SDLCA_FAILED_KEEP_DAYS=30                  # how long kept events (run/failed) are stored; 0 keeps them forever
# SDLCA_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/path/to/.env       # provider API keys, sourced for the agent only (no second copy)
# SDLCA_REPOS=/home/you/repos                # where world clones live: <SDLCA_REPOS>/<owner>/<world>
# SDLCA_GIT_NAME=sdlca-agent                 # commit identity inside world clones
# SDLCA_GIT_EMAIL=sdlca-agent@users.noreply.invalid
